    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0211" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg199"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Bulgaria)/4–2545:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-25T13:00:00+03:00">April 25, 1945—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1341. ReEmbs 244, January 26, 7 p.m. Calling on me April 23 Greek Ambassador
                    stated that as the Soviet Government had not replied to Greek request for
                    representative to Bulgarian ACC he had received instructions from Athens to ask
                    permission for station in liaison office at Sofia to maintain contact with ACC
                    there.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department; repeated to Sofia as 31, Athens as 17, London as 177.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
